{
    "//": [
        "The combined runtime's machine-readable layering contract.",
        "",
        "Before consolidation the package manager made a forbidden layer edge",
        "require a manifest edit. Inside one package this file and lint:layers",
        "replace that enforcement explicitly.",
        "",
        "`mayImport` is exhaustive: a directory may import from itself and from the",
        "layers listed, and from nothing else. Layer names are directory paths, so",
        "the ordering INSIDE global is enforced too -- math is not allowed to reach",
        "sideways into model just because both are global."
    ],
    "surfaces": {
        "index.js": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource",
                "trinity",
                "sof",
                "audio",
                "character",
                "input",
                "core"
            ]
        },
        "global/index.js": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model"
            ]
        }
    },
    "externalImports": [
        "gl-matrix",
        "meshoptimizer",
        "yaml"
    ],
    "externalDynamicImports": [
        "resource/worker/CjsResManWorker.js"
    ],
    "layers": {
        "global/utils": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/math"
            ]
        },
        "global/math": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/consts"
            ]
        },
        "global/consts": {
            "mayImport": []
        },
        "global/compose": {
            "mayImport": []
        },
        "global/schema": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/compose",
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts"
            ]
        },
        "global/model": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/compose",
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/schema"
            ]
        },
        "global/contracts": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/schema"
            ],
            "why": [
                "Contract roots use schema implementation metadata so required",
                "methods carry @impl.abstract as well as their throwing body."
            ]
        },
        "resource": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model"
            ]
        },
        "trinity": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource"
            ]
        },
        "sof": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource"
            ],
            "why": [
                "SOF is standalone and trinity is NOT in its list, which is the whole",
                "point of writing this down. SOF emits a graph that names Trinity and",
                "audio classes; naming a class is not importing it, and a consumer",
                "supplies the constructors. The day someone 'just imports Trinity here'",
                "the build fails instead of the property quietly disappearing."
            ]
        },
        "audio": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource"
            ]
        },
        "character": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource",
                "trinity"
            ]
        },
        "input": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model"
            ]
        },
        "engine/webgpu": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource",
                "trinity"
            ],
            "why": [
                "The implemented backend extends canonical dependency-floor, resource,",
                "and Trinity contracts. It never imports core, tools, or another engine."
            ]
        },
        "core": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils",
                "global/math",
                "global/consts",
                "global/contracts",
                "global/schema",
                "global/model",
                "resource",
                "trinity",
                "sof",
                "audio",
                "character",
                "input",
                "engine/webgpu"
            ],
            "why": [
                "Composition. It is allowed to know about everything below it, which is",
                "exactly why nothing below is allowed to know about it."
            ]
        },
        "tools": {
            "mayImport": [
                "global/utils"
            ],
            "why": [
                "Acquisition only. The demo suite left for the separate",
                "carbonenginejs/demos repository on 2026-08-30, taking the market,",
                "Show Info, Ship Tree, chat, diagram and demo-host families with it;",
                "the realtime wire contract followed once the server lived there too,",
                "and per-object tooling was retired to trinity documentation.",
                "",
                "mayImport is exhaustive, so narrowing it IS the enforcement. Anything",
                "here that needs resource, trinity, or core is not a tool -- it is either",
                "a demo, which belongs in the demos repository, or a runtime value that",
                "belongs lower down."
            ]
        }
    }
}
